<title>NORWAY: Nordics welcome Serb concession, urge human rights.</title>
<headline>Nordics welcome Serb concession, urge human rights.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The five Nordic countries welcomed on Wednesday a decision by Serbian President Slobodan Milosevic to reinstate local election results, but said they would continue to urge him to respect human rights.</p>
<p>&quot;It is positive in itself that Milosevic now has said he will approve of the result of the election, but it must be followed up in practice by concrete measures,&quot; Norwegian Foreign Minister Bjoern Tore Godal said.</p>
<p>Godal was flanked at a news conference by the foreign ministers of Sweden, Denmark, Finland and Iceland following a regular meeting of the ministers.</p>
</text>
